hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16932","He said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Usama ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moving through the people on the day of Hunayn, asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. Then a drunk man was brought, so he ordered those with him to beat him with what was in their hands."
"16933","He said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the campaign of the day of the Conquest, while I was a young lad, moving through the people, asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. Then a drinker was brought, so he ordered them and they beat him with what was in their hands. Among them was one who beat him with a stick, and among them was one who beat him with a whip, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, threw dust upon him."
"16934","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar used to narrate that Khalid ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughira was wounded that day, and he was over the cavalry, the cavalry of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ibn al-Azhar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after Allah defeated the disbelievers and the Muslims returned to their dwellings, walking among the Muslims, saying: Who will guide to the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. He said: So I walked, or he said: So I hastened before him, while I was muhtalim, saying: Who will guide to the dwelling of Khalid, until we alighted at his dwelling, and behold Khalid ibn al-Walid leaning against the back of his saddle. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him and looked at his wound. al-Zuhri said: And I thought he said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, blew upon it. End of the Musnad of the Makkans and Madinans from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah Exalted be pleased with them."
